\\lambda }^{2}+63 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "731c273b-83ef-5ecf-bca7-30fd9429facb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446666} {:answer/id #uuid "75cd4420-20f3-5ded-8c44-39d55a82ae27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446668} {:answer/id #uuid "77ff9bd5-364c-5949-a133-ce7f4bb78ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446670} {:answer/id #uuid "9c38e99e-6b40-58d6-baca-ae8ea0b40eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446684} {:answer/id #uuid "cecd0803-36c1-5916-aeae-507fa6a5a5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446698}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446698} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4615f19-9c7a-5091-99a4-538030c0787d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "86473df3-55aa-5a6b-9f10-9b94fded00fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106988" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}4-\\lambda  & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-9) & =0 \\\\ -12-4\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-1)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1-24 \\\\  & =-23 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be045a5-6b6f-58a1-a9c0-054dd780305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446652} {:answer/id #uuid "680fa24a-7dc3-543d-85de-5db5562557f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446660} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3e29e7-ff34-52ad-a2b3-30b0d4dfc7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446683} {:answer/id #uuid "bb76f2d9-d38e-5ad5-b5ba-f0c456c42a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda +8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446689} {:answer/id #uuid "ee278763-ab63-504f-822f-61b01cf166d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446708}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446652} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff74171-fb77-58e8-9b4d-b1ac71573691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8a11188a-8a0f-5ab5-9de2-8d85b1d9c9bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106954" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-2) & =0 \\\\ 4-\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446742 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee3c296-e699-5a89-9d1d-f1037248664d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446637} {:answer/id #uuid "82038ac4-a96c-5a3c-b35c-2282a0dcbbe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$  (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446672} {:answer/id #uuid "b88cc7bb-ae8f-5c80-a43e-0886bc245383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446688} {:answer/id #uuid "beb9ae44-9c2f-5ff1-949c-f0430bfe2729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446690} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d63c00-47c6-5ea0-81b5-0ff89c996117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446694}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446694} :answer-field/id #uuid "72630b4f-5b3f-5c7f-b8aa-ef29d3000b9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "95ae8df3-3e3d-5382-b3db-f47a4094753f" :question/math-academy-id "q-12293" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle P=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-1\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ 25+5\\lambda +5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+10\\lambda +24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-10\\pm \\sqrt{{10}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 24}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10\\pm \\sqrt{4}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10\\pm 2}{2} \\\\  & =-6,-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b663abe-8ca9-5e98-a421-8ee08f7f4b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446657} {:answer/id #uuid "602aa1ad-6d56-50d3-a5b0-1aeda4a4c661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =18$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446659} {:answer/id #uuid "80774a76-6156-58a8-a1af-8130684f2c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =6$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446671} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfa7309-3f10-57c3-852d-7167399f1f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-18$ and $\\lambda =6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446678} {:answer/id #uuid "f47791cc-1060-50da-baa1-ca82124c18ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =6$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446678} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8c02f9-48d0-57c8-9419-e72e043a5824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c0119bb7-296f-5cbc-ac52-c9d22940b932" :question/math-academy-id "q-107001" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(C-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )(-18-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +18) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-18$ and $\\lambda =6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a787981-8115-531c-a0b2-45614b628dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446651} {:answer/id #uuid "514631b5-18c9-56ed-b862-2cfc925d4f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446655} {:answer/id #uuid "d0015afe-6401-5c12-9cf2-8b51092f7180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446699} {:answer/id #uuid "e79a4073-0867-556b-8d5c-c5025c11ea29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446703} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd3bb9f-f42f-5091-bf4d-48c5dff63db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446715}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446651} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ffc0b3-2fb7-50ab-863d-ef122a417f29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c2d1ce53-250c-556e-b39c-e7210e507a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-106947" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 9 & =0 \\\\ -12-4\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -30 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b5bb84-0f48-5dfe-81a5-5623dd7f6712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446633} {:answer/id #uuid "0d6e90a2-f4f0-5b73-a742-96283d76f4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446636} {:answer/id #uuid "600134d3-9568-5f5f-8691-d69f8a228619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446658} {:answer/id #uuid "ce79e6ac-6a71-5954-97e0-e2449988d58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446697} {:answer/id #uuid "e1884e2a-420c-50b7-a538-8daff46abc19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446702}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446633} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce37090-2b25-52bc-8d16-9e6c6c3f75f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f1a5d1e0-5cd7-522c-a412-852f22ba958a" :question/math-academy-id "q-107844" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =7.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."} {:answer/id #uuid "05141a1b-cb9e-5283-9e45-82ca469a01e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446902} {:answer/id #uuid "13998c82-80d9-5cc7-a5a5-a3c689f79c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446905} {:answer/id #uuid "33a0bdd4-e800-5d6d-849a-fb395e74e06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}({sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446906} {:answer/id #uuid "41e5d50b-2d0d-5687-83c8-c9e67c35fd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446908} {:answer/id #uuid "71985b22-a29a-5e8e-a361-5aa92a2495cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446909} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa86582-4f58-56be-8b2e-64523909f390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446910} {:answer/id #uuid "7b917d8d-ed20-53e9-8f2f-10a316604da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446912} {:answer/id #uuid "bc99ca06-7d50-5d19-b832-2a97e3ac7a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446917} {:answer/id #uuid "cdce5e1a-03fe-5258-9d66-a128329565d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+5{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446918} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0493e8-3b12-50f8-9fc2-390aa24a534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10cd98c4-ea24-55c4-a79c-cf3c9ddf5714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446904} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa86582-4f58-56be-8b2e-64523909f390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446910} {:answer/id #uuid "7b917d8d-ed20-53e9-8f2f-10a316604da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446912} {:answer/id #uuid "bc99ca06-7d50-5d19-b832-2a97e3ac7a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446917} {:answer/id #uuid "d281e271-ac5c-5125-9398-f8102c7c4a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446919}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446910} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3650c47-b992-5daf-9894-5a44218a3232" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2855547f-5d51-5448-b3d2-5e4f3624a47a" :question/math-academy-id "q-51199" :question/problem "![](images/50/5052773d05690f49969487f5ec75a1cdd15c278c1c7552dd5d811ea2e023256c.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $$\n\\displaystyle -\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+1+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+3{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b4071d8-b7bd-5947-891a-3136a4368de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446911} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0e99ea-5dd8-556e-b3e4-bb6d0549ec0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "496b1e54-6c94-5491-8b44-b97586fa418a" :question/math-academy-id "q-353382" :question/problem "![](images/07/07dd1e37f29e06051c7fe84210d41857c7c871ce577c71a86781be4ce7a0ef23.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{(7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{49{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +49{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{49}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}7\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05141a1b-cb9e-5283-9e45-82ca469a01e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446902} {:answer/id #uuid "13998c82-80d9-5cc7-a5a5-a3c689f79c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446905} {:answer/id #uuid "41e5d50b-2d0d-5687-83c8-c9e67c35fd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446908} {:answer/id #uuid "bb736353-f883-5d04-8785-134a0e8d1393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}({4}^{\\pi /2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446916} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0493e8-3b12-50f8-9fc2-390aa24a534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446908} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e112384-cbab-5d5f-b556-741daf47c239" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "53d69396-ad38-5399-a95d-de36a99debd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-103848" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r={4}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={4}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={4}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({4}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({4}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{4}^{2\\theta }+{4}^{2\\theta }{ln}^{2}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1+{ln}^{2}⁡4){4}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{4}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot {4}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot ({4}^{\\pi /2}-{4}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0934e304-801c-5c0d-8b01-386d6337214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446903} {:answer/id #uuid "33a0bdd4-e800-5d6d-849a-fb395e74e06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}({sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446906} {:answer/id #uuid "71985b22-a29a-5e8e-a361-5aa92a2495cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446909} {:answer/id #uuid "b8da428a-8a49-5ad1-b789-ffb6514c0b70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446915} {:answer/id #uuid "cdce5e1a-03fe-5258-9d66-a128329565d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+5{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446918}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446909} :answer-field/id #uuid "48332077-b3d7-5599-9447-7b3caa313948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7a42296f-57b5-52e8-abcc-dbabb67e9573" :question/math-academy-id "q-15121" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{5}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )+25{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea5acb7-0ee2-5efa-9cb6-56917fa73a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446913} {:answer/id #uuid "91b14c4c-3ed0-52f0-a3ee-ae78598ce9a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446914} {:answer/id #uuid "dde56d65-c679-5147-bb10-2f5b7354e62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446920} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d38d23-26ec-5c2a-a257-830016a32749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446921} {:answer/id #uuid "fb78dc11-cc0d-583f-b9e3-429b039a2c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446923}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446923} :answer-field/id #uuid "f44e970c-d097-5c6c-a97c-5ef5ce4b1558" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "954fde1b-bd90-5ee0-826c-b4121bc79ca3" :question/math-academy-id "q-9538" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the polar curve $r=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={2(-2)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =4-2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ebaec30-3483-55e2-9524-7055da0607e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446907} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b76675c-e686-504c-9fa2-4f4538262ff5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f471af72-8928-5fe0-b630-625d8128766a" :question/math-academy-id "q-347923" :question/problem "![](images/81/81632c931b0846520a056a872cdf327b9031fea4e3b91bf2374973fff1a2354b.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=3+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.\n$$*\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{(3+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{9+18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3i}\\sqrt{18+18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =3\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={6\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =12(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =12(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "0d2aeb4a-6148-5344-8241-a30ca0414bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+5{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447092} {:answer/id #uuid "1015c73e-191b-5d23-bc1d-08512f03b481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +8\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447093} {:answer/id #uuid "369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447101} {:answer/id #uuid "39da32fb-4fd3-56f4-8b48-27bfa06dac2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447105} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4c2c76-9822-5adf-bfb2-5991320c3105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }sin\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+6{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\thet