{:answer/id #uuid "48d38326-3827-5037-8c94-f55b16de2521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447107} {:answer/id #uuid "5272c95e-f96d-52e0-9de8-9b6c1893b269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447109} {:answer/id #uuid "59a4d601-d2b3-5c64-9a6e-78d2d155f615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447110} {:answer/id #uuid "acf332da-f102-5954-a0ff-4632294d19b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447110} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d754845-5d58-59c1-864c-f3740c76cc59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1b5a0004-da97-5a43-bf86-5bd3413d5383" :question/math-academy-id "q-123639" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)+{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }|\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{[|-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{2}\\right)|]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}(|-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)|-|-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)|) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "465105e6-5101-55c0-b1d1-06d1ae1a8a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447106} {:answer/id #uuid "8434f6a8-cc90-5b45-b358-8909e66e4e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447116} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea5fefa-7242-5713-8e02-211083d54f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447121} {:answer/id #uuid "9f69be1a-7ddd-5b88-a4da-dc75ecb9eaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447126} {:answer/id #uuid "c6945ce8-db6b-5823-b2dc-01f0875bc633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447126} :answer-field/id #uuid "1943cf7d-279c-5e8f-b1f0-69426fcd72d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "202a66ff-7a74-5355-8081-a73c26b6f2c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-123579" :question/problem "![](images/05/051efe86fa3f118dd82c41f32071982bcdbacbab75212d867a5a809f37506192.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3155478e-1b5a-5e18-bd4c-26ed84959b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447098} {:answer/id #uuid "8234212b-ceff-57f4-a7ce-844e2d396499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447115} {:answer/id #uuid "94931a58-c0c8-5c1d-bfbb-07691dddb8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447123} {:answer/id #uuid "9eeb0c86-cf6c-5ccc-baf9-def02136f813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447125} {:answer/id #uuid "abcd435e-c198-5b6e-9039-b510adba1e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447128}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447125} :answer-field/id #uuid "20dcdcfd-748c-52ae-895b-79a3d2f6200f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "27eda322-b707-5345-adf8-0465217fdeaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-149822" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta (1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17652adb-f0bd-5e06-b55e-fb60b41d8171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447094} {:answer/id #uuid "392cdecf-382d-5eaf-8512-13e93f090b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447104} {:answer/id #uuid "bb292c1a-79be-51a1-91b7-2783d7d709cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447133} {:answer/id #uuid "e84048f5-bc2b-5cb4-a79e-ebf71a21e3cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447139} {:answer/id #uuid "fdef13fa-c9e2-5073-8dc0-04da2e76ab8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447140}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447104} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cca78f2-2d1d-5264-9180-c7409ad32bd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "586f6a61-ad62-56e5-9a2c-611ea0a2819c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123379" :question/problem "![](images/19/19725cfd8068973c899fcb4f54abcebbbfcd24bd68aec510b9d41cee2c2cd02a.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{20-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d7287d-2c86-57db-807a-ce851e800dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447122} {:answer/id #uuid "ad21357d-24c8-5905-9453-f8cf49c4c786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447130} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd8c063-a572-53c2-b4ce-461228304503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447134} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ae75cb-ec9f-5d2a-90c0-9d53665a6116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447136} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8e5566-d63d-5c74-aea1-6e226a17823d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447137}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447137} :answer-field/id #uuid "f262cbb1-b41b-5a16-a002-abeb999c9afc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6947d1ad-4cd9-585a-b94f-f141875b9f2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123581" :question/problem "![](images/36/36008a9155a01a07136cee263ce0a89239719227541536e8c2f8ea358d43e6df.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\cancel{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\cancel{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36dfca93-7965-545e-ae64-ea4e15350f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447102} {:answer/id #uuid "6b63604b-d8a6-599a-838b-2b74c3f0610a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447112} {:answer/id #uuid "76d06d75-8601-5c9f-931a-e187e9f7e576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447113} {:answer/id #uuid "8e346b38-71c5-5bc3-bda7-aa1f806c4b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447120} {:answer/id #uuid "b38cf43c-b624-53ab-921c-a21f0a6ea62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447113} :answer-field/id #uuid "c16bafac-0287-5357-8266-d49db38ec2b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "70661cc4-274a-5311-99fc-fa9cf5ff480d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123426" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2{cos}^{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 3\\pi $ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2{cos}^{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\sqrt{{(2{cos}^{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right))}^{2}+{(-2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\sqrt{{cos}^{6}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)+{cos}^{4}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right){sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)+{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\theta }{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447158 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26a04d3a-0123-57f0-b050-a4cee7844a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{3}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447096} {:answer/id #uuid "3795af39-24b8-5073-90c3-faa50ef95682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447103} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4c2c76-9822-5adf-bfb2-5991320c3105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }sin\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+6{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447108} {:answer/id #uuid "8c59bfa2-430e-5926-995c-ce492668dd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }sin\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1-8{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447119} {:answer/id #uuid "9d63f17c-0ef7-5244-bb03-4939eb982145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{4+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447103} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce35695c-d7ed-5650-b6f0-c0d7e8432851" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7aa4e4d5-0080-5cb6-bebe-9d6c94950127" :question/math-academy-id "q-123511" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\text{ }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{({sin}^{3}\\,\\theta )}^{2}+{(3{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\text{ }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{sin}^{6}\\,\\theta +9{sin}^{4}\\,\\theta \\text{ }\\,{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta +9{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0081acc5-b8a0-5432-9f86-16b58fe1f445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +10\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447091} {:answer/id #uuid "1015c73e-191b-5d23-bc1d-08512f03b481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +8\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447093} {:answer/id #uuid "369565c3-561a-50ca-9be4-d934f4abc68d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447100} {:answer/id #uuid "609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447111} {:answer/id #uuid "8a907a7b-6b1a-50eb-9d99-ac2cfde55650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447111} :answer-field/id #uuid "970ad32f-3bc8-5eae-a83f-06f38e693fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8c80223d-79b2-5d97-8d88-3fa6275a012a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123377" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b8ef36c29d1babc5c3ccf1d474678a18ed5937b883e026d18d5c7ea1aaaa3f5.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +1+8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d2aeb4a-6148-5344-8241-a30ca0414bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+5{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447092} {:answer/id #uuid "369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447101} {:answer/id #uuid "39da32fb-4fd3-56f4-8b48-27bfa06dac2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447105} {:answer/id #uuid "7d101eaf-b053-5e48-a386-fa7d17ca7d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{5+4{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447114} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9bc000-67c4-53d2-b325-fa53d6ea89eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+7{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447101} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8dcb75d-dac3-5c81-8f6e-1e4763779208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fb00dc0e-66fe-5382-b23d-00ac1fa661b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123559" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\pi /3\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2?$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({csc}^{3}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta +9{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta {cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta (1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb4ef7fd-13ca-58f5-a761-f38a0e1a271e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045