98} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475775}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475551} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b9e7048-3689-53e4-bb31-2f73b280aea1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9c15a3d-862e-553a-bd17-8b80866daf10" :question/math-academy-id "q-37694" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf the matrix $A$ above is diagonalizable, find a corresponding diagonal matrix $D.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ by solving $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}7-\\lambda  & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}7-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((7-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )+4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -5)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ (simple root) and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$ (double root).\n\nLet's now find the dimension of the eigenspace corresponding to each eigenvalue.\n\n- First, we consider the simple root ${\\lambda }_{1}=2.$ Since the root is simple, the dimension of the eigenspace ${V}_{2}$ corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{2})=1.\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider the double root ${\\lambda }_{2}=5.$ Let's find the dimension of the eigenspace ${V}_{5}$ corresponding to this eigenvalue. To do this, we row-reduce the matrix $A-5I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-5I & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). This implies that we will have $3-2=1$ linearly independent eigenvector corresponding to the current eigenvalue. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{5})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ is *not* diagonalizable, since \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{2})+\\text{dim}({V}_{5})=1+1=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "428458b7-3340-5fa8-bbfd-d5552b57222e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475542} {:answer/id #uuid "6aab2878-e448-5eb0-91ce-3150b0879bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$A$ is not diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475596} {:answer/id #uuid "b90c159d-7eb3-5ed0-96e5-e1ce483c068a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475721} {:answer/id #uuid "c664f5f4-16ef-516a-8de2-e8c5bd2b781b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475742} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c81f3f-281b-50d3-a9ab-0e5a4f68626b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475742} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4a53fb3-00cc-58aa-aebb-3f7e25363f55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ed2c40c3-1b90-504b-a86e-ac9274a7e945" :question/math-academy-id "q-140315" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf the matrix $A$ above is diagonalizable, find a corresponding diagonal matrix $D.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ by solving $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 8 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )((4-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-8) & =0 \\\\ -(\\lambda -5)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -20) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -5)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ (simple root) and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$ (double root).\n\nLet's now find the dimension of the eigenspace corresponding to each eigenvalue.\n\n- First, we consider the simple root ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4.$ Since the root is simple, the dimension of the eigenspace ${V}_{-4}$ corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{-4})=1.\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider the double root ${\\lambda }_{2}=5.$ Let's find the dimension of the eigenspace ${V}_{5}$ corresponding to this eigenvalue. To do this, we row-reduce the matrix $A-5I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-5I & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). This implies that we will have $3-1=2$ linearly independent eigenvectors corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=5.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{5})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ is diagonalizable, since\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{-4})+\\text{dim}({V}_{5})=1+2=3.\\,✓\n$$\n\nFinally, a corresponding diagonal matrix is \n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3faf9aed-2e42-5804-8239-bab232db5dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477129} {:answer/id #uuid "79b9715e-0243-5db8-8f75-37135a50d142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477130}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477130} :answer-field/id #uuid "a37b91e8-5472-5172-b3e5-dd6ac76e24fa" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477534} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b22226-96da-5ac3-837f-85c6d962014a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-0.927)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477761} {:answer/id #uuid "23b112a7-45d9-59f5-b11b-4a043ad38f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-0.927)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477806} {:answer/id #uuid "d040139f-5db2-5449-b5ff-e7cc5e152405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-0.644)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478148} {:answer/id #uuid "dccbee6a-dd05-5649-ad87-d2d6be5453e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-0.644)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478168} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0972a5-aa0a-506b-9f2d-6cb313e5a657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1.107)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477806} :answer-field/id #uuid "efe9231d-0800-5ee8-8509-d4d9ca580e2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "41ce9e80-1405-5642-831b-08af7169731b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107575" :question/problem "$3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ &=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right) \\\\  & ≈0.927\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(3)^{2}+(4)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-0.927)\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c19d84af-2e7c-52ec-9fb2-1c4d02dfc257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478113}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478113} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a184adc-97c3-5fd4-aa16-2ab651c506af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dc2a00c1-69ff-5ca9-838c-e411473b3c5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-327994" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ &=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(4)^{2}+(3)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ed6854a-cf74-591e-8fe2-00619854ab94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477853} {:answer/id #uuid "454d32d4-5e30-5d47-9068-bb3220f00149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477866} {:answer/id #uuid "8a107828-920e-532b-946a-234e69c84613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478015} {:answer/id #uuid "9788048e-f8b7-5586-af01-ee2107752378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478031} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a20e78-4df7-5e41-99a4-c960fe582b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478015} :answer-field/id #uuid "78daaf88-e999-5da1-8bf1-f099b8191645" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e5e4ccfa-82ff-5c85-afb9-eb5972468216" :question/math-academy-id "q-30579" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ &=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {R}^{2} & =1 \\\\ R & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d8d160-2451-562f-aefd-3db0e0ef0fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478538} {:answer/id #uuid "40d72ac0-a3c5-5832-814d-2a54f2d35d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478539} {:answer/id #uuid "61f86ef2-8183-5115-a218-8fe444974f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7csc⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478542} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe32cdb-ad3d-5087-9b08-760a8593842e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7csc⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478556} {:answer/id #uuid "fc53f318-8fe8-5f6b-9463-9bfceb2b64b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7csc⁡\\theta cot⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478557}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478538} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d93b18b-fb9d-5347-bbbb-727496189eb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "000c3cb5-99b8-5a63-a939-b4c9bbac2e4d" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 7sec⁡\\theta tan⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int sec⁡\\theta tan⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =sec⁡\\theta +C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 7sec⁡\\theta tan⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =7\\int sec⁡\\theta tan⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =7sec⁡\\theta +C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "06006eb6-f76f-5b46-9239-f6620017407b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4csc⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478532} {:answer/id #uuid "17b0b148-43cd-5b9e-b9ab-52f133e6c466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4csc⁡\\theta cot⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478535} {:answer/id #uuid "29d60ffd-ae42-5779-ae82-637a58408d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478536} {:answer/id #uuid "34d8d160-2451-562f-aefd-3db0e0ef0fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478538} {:answer/id #uuid "40d72ac0-a3c5-5832-814d-2a54f2d35d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478539} {:answer/id #uuid "61f86ef2-8183-5115-a218-8fe444974f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7csc⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478542} {:answer/id #uuid "698f8ab9-a102-54d8-a39d-18213c5e7f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478543} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06006eb6-f76f-5b46-9239-f6620017407b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4csc⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478532} {:answer/id #uuid "17b0b148-43cd-5b9e-b9ab-52f133e6c466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4csc⁡\\theta cot⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478535} {:answer/id #uuid "698f8ab9-a102-54d8-a39d-18213c5e7f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478543} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f6dc4a-6bfe-5a65-9bee-fdec047d8685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4csc⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478553} {:answer/id #uuid "eba64cb2-1348-5b3f-950b-db535487607d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4sec⁡\\theta +C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478555}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478555} :answer-field/id #uuid "34c93666-4d9f-5441-a8d7-fa1706238b3d" :answer-field