nswer/id #uuid "d4e0666f-2b5a-53c8-b905-436b08bc6583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487059} {:answer/id #uuid "de845076-a6ce-55d2-9cd1-cde3a48b2d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-\\frac{3}{10}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487077} {:answer/id #uuid "ee425291-e6b5-5c07-9269-4a392656def2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=2\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487101} {:answer/id #uuid "f49f1a1a-8ba9-5ac6-a28d-df18540cdfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487117} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f73ae8d-f2e8-5cf5-bf54-d34ec79a90c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=3\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486690} {:answer/id #uuid "34e09dab-11a6-5462-9d88-bddc2bd9213b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$inf(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486707} {:answer/id #uuid "42fc1632-c9c1-5009-88f7-185a50c722d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=3\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486738} {:answer/id #uuid "c019112a-3b1b-5e5d-bb33-cb7e429db013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487019} {:answer/id #uuid "f49f1a1a-8ba9-5ac6-a28d-df18540cdfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487019} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d4e4ded-e058-51a6-b1cd-e47d3c47538e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "13b42a92-bc61-5733-b661-85ce69e84b97" :question/math-academy-id "q-253513" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{3-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=3-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/35/351e7bb3db6811be2a690fbd3fc2dc99282c4ff676e9116717d85515a298cf80.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is increasing and converges to $3.$ The minimum of $A$ is \n\n$$\nmin(A)={a}_{1}=3-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{1}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $x\\le {a}_{1}$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $x>{a}_{1}$ cannot be a lower bound because ${a}_{1},$ an element of $A,$ is smaller than $x.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{2}]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{2}]=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\frac{5}{2}$ is the minimum of $A.$ Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ninf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\in A.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e00bd87d-5f08-5393-9463-9cdcd001373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487081}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487081} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c08a640-f274-5c79-a1a1-0eb159327882" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1a350bae-823f-50ee-90ca-2add36d5d3d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-253896" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d745d274250c84f6701ff22d17d0c6506a9f03f4a1a461e09f609a0ea11d99b.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=[-2,1).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 1$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<1$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $y$ for any $y<1.$\n\nTherefore, $[1,\\infty )$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[1,\\infty )=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "089cddaa-aa6b-5dcb-bd04-ae36f98a9046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486611} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0beefd6-38b7-58b0-b684-3936a2521ce3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "546541ff-37d6-5bb0-b37e-29f5b9d47681" :question/math-academy-id "q-253541" :question/problem "What is the infimum of the set $B=\\{-0.15,\\,-0.2,\\,0.05,\\,0,\\,9\\}?$\n\n$inf(B)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a set $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B.$\n\nIf $B$ is a finite set, the infimum of $B$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}inf(B) & =min\\{-0.15,\\,-0.2,\\,0.05,\\,0,\\,9\\}=-0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9361e261-f15d-591a-931f-9e610bd52ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486918}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486918} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca91595e-71b1-5317-89fa-84ff2c24db93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56e0e5d9-1f02-588c-913a-41be6c70db4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-252987" :question/problem "What is the supremum of the set $A=\\{-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2\\}?$\n\n$sup(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2\\}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a10166f-357f-5f79-8588-8f1e9cacb997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486824}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486824} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df0afb2-d916-50c2-9c1a-18d1e73450fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5d279c4a-988e-5c29-a6a0-5c2bb436ded0" :question/math-academy-id "q-253550" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\frac{1}{5-n}:n\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the supremum of $A?$\n\n$sup(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. \n\nFirst, let's write down all the terms of our set by substituting $n=1,2,3,4$ into the expression for the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5-0} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-1} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-3} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1\\}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cdb8be-ff0a-5ba1-b0a9-dc08786b5ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486810} {:answer/id #uuid "780a734c-73b7-5ed7-8224-36e0b8d09502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486857} {:answer/id #uuid "ae00c5e2-c9f7-5933-9796-5ffc94c34d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486983} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b738d0-d9f1-569e-acb9-261c8fe2e4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486810} :answer-field/id #uuid "17cc1735-bda1-5b2e-bec3-aadf0a63ced6" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487145} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0735ca12-5065-5046-b0f7-3bfc9e3f9c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486606} {:answer/id #uuid "336b7dfe-4cdb-510d-86ba-babad133fa08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486703} {:answer/id #uuid "8111b881-fedc-53ac-8138-d5cb476af676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486875} {:answer/id #uuid "8804212c-b06e-5ca9-99c5-91c09337b300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486889}] :an