swer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df18746-d758-5a09-ba93-5a96091a3485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486682} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1d4f54-ba66-5d74-b830-bebeeaccc756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486760} {:answer/id #uuid "7655aeae-96f8-5e53-9aa1-841686422a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486850} {:answer/id #uuid "debfbc3c-489a-5590-b118-2dcd9348b992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487078}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487078} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae07e5e5-6e19-529b-9f50-bceccec9dd57" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e871b676-2c06-50d7-81b0-8662a3a9169b" :question/math-academy-id "q-253041" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=[0,\\infty ).$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(A)$ and $sup(A).$\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(A)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $A$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(A)$ {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A,$ and the supremum is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le 0$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,0]$ contains only lower bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>0$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>0.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,0]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,0]=0.\n$$\n\nNext, to find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSince $A$ is unbounded above, $A$ has no upper bounds, and $sup(A)=+\\infty .$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of a set $A$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $A,$ and the supremum is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ is $\\text{bounded below},$ we have $inf(A)=0.$\n\nSince $A$ is $\\text{unbounded above},$ we have $sup(A)=+\\infty .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6e4397-fca7-502a-957d-5547a9e1e822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486619} {:answer/id #uuid "35622caa-ce19-5bfc-a7fa-dc9d8b125e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486708} {:answer/id #uuid "97202376-a3bb-5501-989d-ca966878311d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486932} {:answer/id #uuid "b4173517-8f8f-5114-8e3b-aabe602f41c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486932} :answer-field/id #uuid "0141976c-ee04-53f0-9dd6-35986d4022e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074ead33-f8e0-5fdd-b4f5-980c95e11480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486608} {:answer/id #uuid