pe {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486770} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2c93e6-9906-55a9-8413-428b71166395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486869}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486624} :answer-field/id #uuid "98631c3a-b7b8-5e51-9528-4755eb8c1bc1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487222} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "201ceafe-9cde-510e-94f6-947e5d6472b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486657} {:answer/id #uuid "63734a92-b3f1-59c8-9eb8-2fd264d2bb50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486813} {:answer/id #uuid "94c16107-81fc-53a0-9f76-3bb3d8bfa2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486920} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2db595-99a3-57f2-9df2-ccb0175a7e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486979}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486920} :answer-field/id #uuid "a40b4703-dfd5-5604-aa4e-aadffb8912d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f40d36d-d2b7-5cc9-a838-0f50f4cd9b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486765} {:answer/id #uuid "9689b929-527a-52d4-a206-485a73c02b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486928} {:answer/id #uuid "bd29a704-1486-51d5-b294-3cbf1133db31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487008} {:answer/id #uuid "be630098-5226-5121-b2a6-8716ace79205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487015}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487008} :answer-field/id #uuid "f44a72e2-fb07-5479-a992-4153e0e61bf3" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f25266f1-2830-5a2e-9d12-da4f0e084a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-253561" :question/problem "Consider the set $B=(-\\infty ,\\pi \\,].$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(B)$ and $sup(B).$\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the {{field-1}} of $B,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(B)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(B)$ {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B,$ and the supremum is the smallest upper bound of $B.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSince $B$ is unbounded below, $B$ has no lower bounds, and $inf(B)=-\\infty .$\n\nNext, to find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge \\pi $ is greater than or equal to the elements of $B.$ Thus, the set $[\\pi ,\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $B.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<\\pi $ is **not** an upper bound of $B.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $B$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, $[\\pi ,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $B,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(B)=min\\,[\\pi ,\\infty )=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of a set $B$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $B,$ and the supremum is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is $\\text{unbounded below},$ we have $inf(B)=-\\infty .$\n\nSince $B$ is $\\text{bounded above},$ we have $sup(B)=\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d7b7700-3e95-510c-a153-82350219ac3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$inf(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486620} {:answer/id #uuid "65aa0c48-3279-5f91-ae4c-1449b2527192" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486818} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ad51fd-d8f5-59d7-8e16-ad0e1d154496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-\\frac{3}{10}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487020} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e0666f-2b5a-53c8-b905-436b08bc6583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487059} {:answer/id #uuid "de845076-a6ce-55d2-9cd1-cde3a48b2d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-\\frac{3}{10}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487059} :answer-field/id #uuid "73153ef3-6520-50a9-82e3-ddb42b9894a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd2b3866-cbeb-5f5a-bcbc-008f4c1cdcd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-253912" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{-1+{\\left(\\frac{7}{10}\\right)}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-1+{\\left(\\frac{7}{10}\\right)}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/8b/8be6d8824c8cbf1fb66d64d3ccc027f2949149adc9f95cf4d1f3a814baec80b3.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing and converges to $-1.$ \n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number in the set $x\\le -1$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number in the set $x>-1$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find a sufficiently large $n$ so that $-1+{\\left(\\frac{7}{10}\\right)}^{n}$ is smaller than $x$ for any $x>-1.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-1]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-1]=-1.\n$$\n\nNotice that $-1$ is *not* the minimum of $A$ (the set $A$ has no minimum). Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ninf(A)=-1\\notin A.\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "128ee1a2-ad98-5075-846f-b8cbe5627a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{7}{4}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487604} {:answer/id #uuid "275267aa-7fe6-5509-801e-f9b125fe4ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$inf(B)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487649} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6fc4ae-7a22-54f3-b550-cb820c80a006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(B)=-1\\in B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487756} {:answer/id #uuid "7d320ab4-e7ea-5b1a-9b1e-fcd8c46760b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487808} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac9b3db-343c-58f0-83db-0523448093be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=1\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487857} {:answer/id #uuid "a578b96c-4dcd-5d98-afab-f309822e5646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(B)=2\\in B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487876} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f6d5db-d453-51b2-81bf-72bad96c4aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value