ref 17592186488618} {:answer/id #uuid "590bf0de-aa9c-5cf8-b6b6-eb31e0700ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488640} {:answer/id #uuid "5e011c7d-1483-5d78-9bc4-5f179586ff35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=3\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488651} {:answer/id #uuid "72f49a2a-7e33-5dea-8248-8b07b4770499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-5\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488700} {:answer/id #uuid "8695d407-b8e6-5951-8447-a9dc025727b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=5\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488734} {:answer/id #uuid "93a7b3b0-bb34-5a9f-a039-8842eb3f070b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-5\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488766} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d0eb3a-5dc4-5b58-944e-b28df01e747b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=7\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488807} {:answer/id #uuid "ae14740c-0bec-5b4d-9e98-d2aa11f93eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$inf(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488816} {:answer/id #uuid "b98431df-8366-56c8-bb4a-a0335b0aa79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{13}{2}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488839} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4faa51-f0ba-59dd-a17c-8673a8ed7588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{21}{5}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488926} {:answer/id #uuid "e27c7066-6cee-5bf3-8410-52b38d657725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=0\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488941} {:answer/id #uuid "f17c6a34-e689-50a4-8b50-91c915977c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{21}{5}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488981} {:answer/id #uuid "fef7ef80-e0c5-5157-bd1a-b6b0059c3156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489014} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424cb1f4-7e81-5741-9fea-91a70c42cb72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{13}{2}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488607} {:answer/id #uuid "4c403958-65ff-5e3d-a88d-eb4c593bbb86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=7\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488618} {:answer/id #uuid "590bf0de-aa9c-5cf8-b6b6-eb31e0700ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488640} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d0eb3a-5dc4-5b58-944e-b28df01e747b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=7\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488807} {:answer/id #uuid "b98431df-8366-56c8-bb4a-a0335b0aa79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{13}{2}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488839}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488618} :answer-field/id #uuid "11588f66-7282-571e-8e23-97b1f1c241fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "03070e45-f0e3-5991-b98c-709745709961" :question/math-academy-id "q-253526" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{7-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=7-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/ca/cae6f56db55b49b98df6ce7e3ae0777e725af14de9dedb5b61b54039bac41860.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is increasing and converges to $7.$ \n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number in the set $x\\ge 7$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number in the set $x<7$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find a sufficiently large $n$ so that $7-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{n}$ is greater than $x$ for any $x<7.$\n\nTherefore, $[7,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[7,\\infty )=7.\n$$\n\nNotice that $7$ is *not* the maximum of $A$ (the set $A$ has no maximum). Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nsup(A)=7\\notin A.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d76112fe-0fce-56ee-bf7a-c6fba9800dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488914}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488914} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed2c775-df54-54e2-ad43-b85dd389a975" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "42308119-ffcd-55c6-b052-68e017e7cc90" :question/math-academy-id "q-253897" :question/problem "![](images/64/64131e649a82e06d2750d53bdf05b1701b0674a05b70149081ddb58d700adb54.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,2).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 2$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<2$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $y$ for any $y<2.$\n\nTherefore, $[2,\\infty )$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[2,\\infty )=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae27d87-d1eb-5508-9fca-440370a0760d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488562} {:answer/id #uuid "acc9f243-7017-5914-9e36-38110bd0f43d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488812} {:answer/id #uuid "f409a862-986f-5f72-b38f-9785d600adce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488985} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1c810a-8c08-59ba-b916-0dd9d63ae793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488985} :answer-field/id #uuid "735af475-5f6e-5f4d-94ac-fce00a40be32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13913c42-5790-55ea-9c27-2f99664ad2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488513} {:answer/id #uuid "9df3259e-42b9-5784-955e-560ae10f25fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488781} {:answer/id #uuid "eeacc765-06e6-57eb-ae18-7ea5ea284084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488970} {:answer/id #uuid "fe52fb74-c34e-5ecb-addb-23025f829a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489011}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488781} :answer-field/id #uuid "97af60c6-81d5-5dcc-8fd8-64c597a89cac" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7f80cf-6432-5a5d-bd8f-198372c4b57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=2\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488560} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa831a5-e26c-5fdf-887e-7810e8926c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=0\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488590} {:answer/id #uuid "401f2f06-e683-5990-b8a2-42733884b2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488601} {:answer/id #uuid "4048a7cf-5e90-517d-b59e-7c8fe9d1d965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=2\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488603} {:answer/id #uuid "e27c7066-6cee-5bf3-8410-52b38d657725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=0\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488941}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488603} :answer-field/id #uuid "c36b9a2c-4e62-5b21-9012-7faf214bd6f7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7013dafc-513b-5282-9b6e-8298bbcaa96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488693} {:answer/id #uuid "efa4a326-17fa-5372-b69d-5e6405b0fba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488693} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc061c6-f499-57fc-948d-02e770903359" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8283d19d-ef90-50f2-bc41-5e0573a21b42" :question/math-academy-id "q-253512" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=(0,2).$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $sup(A).$\n\nThe supremum of a set $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge 2$ is greater than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $[2,\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<2$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<2.$\n\nTherefore, $[2,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[2,\\infty )=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that $2\\notin A.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe supremum of $A$ is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $A.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\ge 2\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $sup(A)=2\\notin A.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02cd44fe-73ba-5cc5-888a-532c8eaa56c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=5\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488474} {:answer/id #uuid "72f49a2a-7e33-5dea-8248-8b07b4770499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-5\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488700} {:answer/id #uuid "8695d407-b8e6-5951-8447-a9dc025727b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=5\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488734} {:answer/id #uuid "93a7b3b0-bb34-5a9f-a039-8842eb3f070b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "inf(A)=-5\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488766} {:answer/id #uuid "ae14740c-0bec-5b4d-9e98-d2aa11f93eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$inf(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488816}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488700} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6ccc5e-e2f1-5031-9908-8c3a1cc535d6" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ff16d2b-088f-58fd-ae03-0c295e84321a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488691} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb7c0f0-a427-5e99-9e1c-6f64c7231523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488887} {:answer/id #uuid "d887ad99-aa6e-5862-87f6-ff4b2afd5cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488918} {:answer/id #uuid "f890a2ad-8c82-5d77-9676-cf64f7dae8f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488995}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488887} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c45689-30e7-585c-ad39-8fbbfb0111be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f2aab30-7cdd-5e6a-b89c-3a778d1501a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488688} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c9bf2b-ccef-54f9-8489-828f4a946872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488822}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488688} :answer-field/id #uuid "e67fda2f-7168-5347-a8d3-f53e8a1874eb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225422b7-65e9-5615-8767-2543d225f63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488539} {:answer/id #uuid "a21eac77-4a8d-5a1a-a8b3-704e5197e4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488790} {:answer/id #uuid "b2347c38-baed-5481-b764-dca5a77c4889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488826} {:answer/id #uuid "d62ffa3e-3570-5c8f-89e2-cacd170877a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488790} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa87f6a-f0a6-55ea-84b0-cbaaaa5fa7b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "993667c9-c973-5dd1-b35f-eb1848f951dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-253557" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=(-5,5].$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $inf(A).$\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le -5$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,-5]$ contains only lower bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>-5$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>-5.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-5]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-5]=-5.\n$$\n\nNotice that $-5\\notin A.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $A.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\le -5\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $inf(A)=-5\\notin A.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ca890c-4ce7-564d-a6a4-a9bac71abb91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=3\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488487} {:answer/id #uuid "5e011c7d-1483-5d78-9bc4-5f179586ff35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=3\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488651} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4faa51-f0ba-59dd-a17c-8673a8ed7588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{21}{5}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488926} {:answer/id #uuid "f17c6a34-e689-50a4-8b50-91c915977c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{21}{5}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488981} {:answer/id #uuid "fef7ef80-e0c5-5157-bd1a-b6b0059c3156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488926} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7ca4c4c-da25-5075-bde9-61051e330507" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c7f8c921-7225-588c-b9e8-a78affb7e519" :question/math-academy-id "q-253843" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{3+2{\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=3+2{\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/05/05737c6e8e7b88f1a91a5fd6cc7d5b6a088227e327ef66e937e279c090a47256.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing and converges to $3.$ The maximum of $A$ is \n\n$$\nmax(A)={a}_{1}=3+2{\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)}^{1}=\\frac{21}{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $x\\ge {a}_{1}$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $x<{a}_{1}$ cannot be an upper bound because ${a}_{1},$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $x.$\n\nTherefore, $[\\frac{21}{5},\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[\\frac{21}{5},\\infty )=\\frac{21}{5}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\frac{21}{5}$ is the maximum of $A.$ Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nsup(A)=\\frac{21}{5}\\in A.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b8257c3-cb89-57e7-af23-191b90a42228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488647}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488647} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ad18e2-13e5-50fe-b40b-8175f7273995" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd9f0c45-62d6-5bab-b897-93c9f4793a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-253869" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5dc63d364beae0482fdb996372e5042e4c5edf2a6bdbd7a5b79dbcc55cf419cb.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,4].$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 4$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<4$ cannot be an upper bound of $A$ because $4,$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $y.$\n\nTherefore, $[4,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[4,\\infty )=4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac2a3d6-1261-55ae-9429-ab0a45e319bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x{sin}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489395} {:answer/id #uuid "3979ed87-af85-57db-8316-21223ec16943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489399} {:answer/id #uuid "5326b014-bdff-590c-91fd-da791559ff94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489405} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c86454-1fbf-57d8-9fab-f0e9a82e9af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489443} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dc7484-013b-5097-9937-5df5cca67819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489449}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489449} :answer-field/id #uuid "a31723c2-df16-5a29-a9cf-4ab545f80f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2168b13d-cc27-5e92-a481-beee5381eccc" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{3},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v=1{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=3{u}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1))^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1))\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =6x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "22005ee4-41d0-5760-b893-f0fac19db39a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489393} {:answer/id #uuid "2970eeb1-3b49-50db-9453-4ae0d788a789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12\\operatorname{cot}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489394} {:answer/id #uuid "2ac2a3d6-1261-55ae-9429-ab0a45e319bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x{sin}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489395} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2a9975-b462-5030-bd6f-57419893c0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1{cot}^{3}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489396} {:answer/id #uuid "3979ed87-af85-57db-8316-21223ec16943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489399} {:answer/id #uuid "5326b014-bdff-590c-91fd-da791559ff94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489405} {:answer/id #uuid "5c23db35-1c82-59b5-adbb-2c1801e613c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489407} {:answer/id #uuid "607877ee-30d1-5662-a148-072bd2a65e8a" :answe