egin{aligned}\n\\int\\sech^2\\left(\\frac{5x}{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=1\\int\\sech^2 u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=1\\tanh u+C \\\\\n&=1\\tanh\\left(\\frac{5x}{5}\\right)+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe argument is linear and the integrand is defined for every real $x$."} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c8b8a6-3940-5b4f-a185-ff227446647f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4(\\sech 2 - \\sech 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490462} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a543f6-2945-5db7-8563-0d4a53675fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\csch^{2} \\left(\\frac{1x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490464} {:answer/id #uuid "bf434d9b-4a7a-5ef1-af0d-672c641490be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}(\\sech 7 - \\sech 14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490467} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030c3210-41d0-5d61-908e-6a5256cd4f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\tanh \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right)\\sech \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490413} {:answer/id #uuid "1a7625a0-da78-5b93-988d-411851e95bf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\tanh^{2} \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490416} {:answer/id #uuid "4e90ae45-661d-54de-a0ba-beeb24ace4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490431} {:answer/id #uuid "7f134b14-df14-5b6f-8f49-59aa902f5ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\tanh \\left(\\frac{5x}{6}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490444} {:answer/id #uuid "f313c669-3bcc-5d7a-8bcb-6c8ac49990b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}\\csch^{2} \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490478}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490431} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce095602-03dd-5b07-943d-af6c81a7c8d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bfb61a77-a546-509b-9714-acf060d2c17a" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int\\sech^{2} \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{6x}{5}$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUsing the substitution and $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\tanh u=\\sech^2 u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sech^2\\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\int\\sech^2 u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh u+C \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{6}\\tanh\\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right)+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe argument is linear and the integrand is defined for every real $x$."} {:answer/id #uuid "c09f13ab-5b50-5146-b98b-2f23e96ea05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(\\sech 8 - \\sech 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490469} {:answer/id #uuid "d418fdcd-5f31-530f-899f-e7240d74ca22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(\\sech 2 - \\sech 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490472} {:answer/id #uuid "d6baf139-0216-57c5-8f75-c6bffa001d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}\\tanh \\left(\\frac{4x}{5}\\right)\\sech \\left(\\frac{4x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490473} {:answer/id #uuid "f313c669-3bcc-5d7a-8bcb-6c8ac49990b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}\\csch^{2} \\left(\\frac{6x}{5}\\right) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f64a5c-9e09-59b8-b17f-a73c876d2ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{sin}^{3}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490488}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490488} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddbff81c-389a-5289-971d-8139b0252065" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "140dd45d-8107-5dae-9564-2bd6cb1a4f7b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={sin}^{4}⁡(x),$ we have\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =4{sin}^{3}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "15ed3388-c369-5661-8011-9ad85b8a7185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{sin}^{5}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ed3388-c369-5661-8011-9ad85b8a7185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{sin}^{5}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490485} {:answer/id #uuid "1fefddaa-9b00-592c-976c-b15111b07144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{cos}^{5}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490487} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccb1a92-1ab5-55f6-a051-1d41270340a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{cos}^{5}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490489} {:answer/id #uuid "c7a2b12a-811a-5b4b-be9f-b7b864c872c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{cos}^{5}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490494} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1ebebb-65a6-537a-9641-f6753ff84f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{sin}^{5}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490496}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490494} :answer-field/id #uuid "93ee8452-84d9-53fa-945b-db9c9f23d54d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1da4f94b-c6e6-57bb-95c9-efc33159af10" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{6},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=6{u}^{5}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =6{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6{u}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-6{cos}^{5}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "1fefddaa-9b00-592c-976c-b15111b07144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{cos}^{5}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490487} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccb1a92-1ab5-55f6-a051-1d41270340a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{cos}^{5}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490489} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67b6c87a-70ca-5491-baa9-b7ba9b113855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175