:question/math-academy-id "q-96018" :question/problem "$$\n\\int (3+2{sech}^{2}⁡w)\\,\\text{d}w=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}w}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡w)={sech}^{2}⁡w\\,⇒\\,\\int {sech}^{2}⁡w\\,\\text{d}w=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡w+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3+2{sech}^{2}⁡w)\\,\\text{d}w & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}w+\\int 2{sech}^{2}⁡w\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}w+2\\int {sech}^{2}⁡w\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =3w+2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡w+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc1200a-020e-579b-aeb4-32e6f6dd2ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514904} {:answer/id #uuid "22fc55f5-eece-5862-9495-0d348b157ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514954} {:answer/id #uuid "46cb26bc-9466-528b-b53b-aa32a469316e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515021} {:answer/id #uuid "8faee535-6239-5c50-8da1-ab3ca13c3eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515178} {:answer/id #uuid "c42c37da-db11-55f7-a6fa-ee35d397e0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{csch}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515288}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515178} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fcaf6c9-8a15-52b1-a33f-3f4796a6e58a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "58b4a157-5f9c-5f77-a21d-1b131c8f0140" :question/math-academy-id "q-95450" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(-{csch}^{2}⁡x)-(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c6288c-a7a5-5339-b54b-1574f3d6b867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x(2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515024} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf54fd4-6b0f-50ff-a220-778bd198efc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515097} {:answer/id #uuid "8a431668-bf6d-5679-ae3b-f87922954d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515159} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9c404c-45ca-5797-a6b2-587a4722a97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515280} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c2ee11-1fdd-5116-b3c9-c3625f9cb203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x(2\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515379}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515280} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee35a739-301f-5040-bed9-e710c7640e85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "598d9b4b-1def-5b7e-8724-7abe41dc985d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95585" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x)=2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot (-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-2{x}^{3}{csch}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a4049a-fca7-5f52-bfb1-771580341b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514910} {:answer/id #uuid "15ccd49d-999f-5394-bd85-dc0b8b867ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514919} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd04e6e-2a4a-5265-b550-0dcfb916da3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514971} {:answer/id #uuid "4ace196d-01ef-57ff-8b7f-750161ecd9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515038} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e6f4e6-23c8-5da2-a89b-5234a110c448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515383}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514971} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3c01d9-f6b5-59af-9a9b-7d7b991856a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6cac54f6-b1ee-5704-8eb2-39e7e0d78de0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95893" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overbrace{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)}^{g(x)}}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e61680f-34d0-54c9-a581-fc46337f2489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x{sech}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515045} {:answer/id #uuid "c2870e74-3428-5720-b294-4aedf55aa1a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}{csch}^{2}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515285} {:answer/id #uuid "c853cba8-3165-56c6-a436-2b32f112bafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515297} {:answer/id #uuid "d5214c15-24d4-5045-a3fa-cdf23f818462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x{csch}^{2}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515319} {:answer/id #uuid "e6496d12-4f39-58a0-bc57-cd3eaaeb3ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{coth}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515297} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdada9a0-319d-50fa-a0c4-8211688157c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "76beb3b0-dbd8-5192-b70b-0a4bac401337" :question/math-academy-id "q-95570" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\\,g={x}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-{csch}^{2}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18df1be8-527c-5a6e-9f98-b10d18413d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514927} {:answer/id #uuid "2d38c782-b76b-5f2e-9bc1-52a75a14aae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}(1-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sech}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514972} {:answer/id #uuid "5df3b1cb-49c5-5619-b74d-771d324baa71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}(1+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515078} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e88966-4166-5138-ba39-d7f1856ad0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515217} {:answer/id #uuid "d89ce40e-349e-5c17-89d4-b56369e8b9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514927} :answer-field/id #uuid "c01224a1-e3b1-57d5-aa15-96438779d2bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7b044358-869c-54b8-ba0e-868b6f91f848" :question/math-academy-id "q-95581" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot (-2x{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515569 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049fa100-40fb-558d-a706-98cb51270374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514883} {:answer/id #uuid "8548fcd7-b1dc-55d8-b576-44ec1a1cb5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515148} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbb7054-2e28-56a6-ac8b-4a4516f8e59f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515201} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a6cb95-2d20-5064-94c1-f104d506b1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515350} {:answer/id #uuid "eafd044b-db1b-5753-972f-0c09ea3f5918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515148} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a0d20a-e247-5de6-9e87-dc2aa68c5128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8386701e-f444-5c82-8928-9b7b2e5dd7d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95892" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overbrace{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}^{g(x)}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3017d4ed-3882-520b-a996-9fdf270542a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x+x{tanh}^{2}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514980} {:answer/id #uuid "59f86a6e-f337-50e8-81fb-3fddff5be091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{x}^{2}{tanh}^{2}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515074} {:answer/id #uuid "759f1f90-6344-577e-9bac-c36fc6f545db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(1-x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515114} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2b53d9-b9f2-5c4b-a6ff-2d9c5e028405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515230} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fb8197-f137-5a59-878a-191936644f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-x{tanh}^{2}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515256}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515230} :answer-field/id #uuid "9407eea0-1e45-5270-a47d-8ad06eaf5ea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9031fff8-a36e-5cc9-9588-e90f1f428aa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95889" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}(-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "291fa27b-e8d1-5ed7-8fbf-082f5be7a7e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514968} {:answer/id #uuid "490d959f-b059-5325-8c05-c4b0cc600f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515030} {:answer/id #uuid "58d6b2ae-f213-5a45-acf0-0b0f01d98283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515071} {:answer/id #uuid "73b4e303-9008-5e9e-855f-481e71c7524e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515110} {:answer/id #uuid "9c149e2c-33ae-5abe-b943-9a619752febc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515203}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515030} :answer-field/id #uuid "78bb2f4a-9757-595a-a198-758752968458" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b84615c0-35fb-546b-b311-f278e0c613e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-95478" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61276995-74bd-5344-aa45-015217ab0d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515081} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd2715d-56f1-531c-9661-a9c48c9057cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515096} {:answer/id #uuid "78513305-089d-5926-bd36-dc21c4328d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515121} {:answer/id #uuid "8b54fd43-f7d2-592e-902d-5621425e00b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515163} {:answer/id #uuid "e944c330-fa87-5fb5-b030-527351a8f08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sech}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515364}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515163} :answer-field/id #uuid "33fef8da-1fed-575c-b52c-5735f185e8df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b9b1e144-f837-55bf-a0c3-8113231511af" :question/math-academy-id "q-95577" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x)=2{sech}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=2{g}^{2},\\,g=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4g(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515598 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3913e98d-6f83-56d3-91d7-ff2f32e15e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514996} {:answer/id #uuid "3aeb0a67-56ca-5962-8e3b-7bedc6372910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515002} {:answer/id #uuid "4902412c-0550-564e-869c-3d3c7116bee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515029} {:answer/id #uuid "56341777-5636-52fc-a550-48d78387c058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515065} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0fce6e-25a6-5623-a414-4de231b8bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515168}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514996} :answer-field/id #uuid "98f39c56-36d9-5e09-95c9-775d62585187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c8cdc03f-da95-544a-8d8d-7ede702d3109" :question/math-academy-id "q-96051" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,⇒\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14996826-58fd-5f33-872c-ee218d66b803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x{coth}^{2}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514916} {:answer/id #uuid "2079f812-1687-58bc-84c8-a6540751137c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514946} {:answer/id #uuid "544fd53c-bf80-59a4-b498-861dbea14ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515059} {:answer/id #uuid "79f1e788-3c2d-59d8-a0bf-2ec512ab473a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(2x{coth}^{2}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515126} {:answer/id #uuid "c46b8049-5168-58e4-97c5-3a3c60907ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+2x{coth}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515291}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515059} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a955475-a532-56de-a95a-903c6b5439c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ca80da50-025a-555f-9c99-42892fcfd87d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95588" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x)=-3x{csch}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=-3x$ and $v(x)={csch}^{2}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3x)}^{′}\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x+(-3x)\\cdot {({csch}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x-3x\\cdot (2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3{csch}^{2}⁡x+6x{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27eb7323-cc8e-5eb9-884b-240fb1bdb83f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{sech}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514964} {:answer/id #uuid "28420209-4741-5df8-9bcf-b3d002b845fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514967} {:answer/id #uuid "71c8a2a8-ead0-50d5-ad25-c720628db79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515105} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7f1c28-26fb-571d-b34a-d848f93d4078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515272} {:answer/id #uuid "ded027e6-96f7-5da7-a4e2-77b340d6cc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514967} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1235ebd-5a71-577a-ad30-6fbc32ad0509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e0bc8c85-75bd-5d02-9581-c62ed55b672c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95481" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=6\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6{csch}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31205a45-c043-5151-9538-0cb51610df28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515746} {:answer/id #uuid "4445012b-a30a-562d-96a0-7dcef2da30c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9} + 2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515758} {:answer/id #uuid "5f87a3d9-e94b-5c58-9b94-d8182a17e886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9} + 2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515763} {:answer/id #uuid "6dfcc9ff-fc82-5d08-b3f8-66d629ce51dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515771} {:answer/id #uuid "a8babb1f-fd7f-50e0-a213-e006d39036ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515746} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0449070-b0e7-51f1-b586-8fb2f5b424b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1383763d-65fc-5f85-a16a-c07b5229168b" :question/problem "If $\\tan x = \\frac{4}{9}$, then $\\tan (-x + 2π) =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x+2\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\tan (-x + 2π)=-\\frac{4}{9}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0721319b-127f-5b39-9735-d2984e422940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5} - 7π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515737} {:answer/id #uuid "3488d6c6-82c6-5eb4-85e5-7079fe5e8f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{5} - 7π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515747} {:answer/id #uuid "431bf0c5-82c3-5aa9-8c62-2d681f941701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515757} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9c5511-3979-545f-94ca-de2b60fb12be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515775} {:answer/id #uuid "f253e2ae-3f1c-5e89-b635-07673f25de9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515805}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515805} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ae739ec-bf10-532f-b188-9f8498b387c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2a4929bf-d737-567f-9af5-55c791cb6e1c" :question/problem "If $\\tan x = \\frac{9}{5}$, then $\\tan (-x - 7π) =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\tan (-x - 7π)=-\\frac{9}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d5985b1-90fb-523b-bdad-f972630acc1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515753} {:answer/id #uuid "926faefa-4